---
title: "certificate_formation (Sui Whitepaper: Transaction Certificate Lifecycle)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_user_sign: user signs transaction Tx with private key
    q_user_sign --> q_send_authorities: send Tx to Sui authorities (keyless from here)

    q_send_authorities --> q_collect_signs: authorities validate and return TxSign
    q_collect_signs --> q_check_quorum: check if quorum of authority stake reached

    q_check_quorum --> q_collect_signs: quorum not yet reached, wait for more responses
    q_check_quorum --> q_form_cert: quorum reached (> 2/3 total stake)

    q_form_cert --> q_create_txcert: collate TxSign into TxCert (transaction certificate)
    q_create_txcert --> q_send_cert: send TxCert back to all authorities

    q_send_cert --> q_authorities_exec: authorities process certificate and execute
    q_authorities_exec --> q_collect_eff: collect EffSign from authorities

    q_collect_eff --> q_check_eff_quorum: check if quorum of effect signatures reached
    q_check_eff_quorum --> q_collect_eff: quorum not yet reached
    q_check_eff_quorum --> q_form_eff_cert: quorum reached

    q_form_eff_cert --> q_finality: create EffCert (effects certificate) as proof of finality
    q_finality --> [*]: transaction is final

    note right of q_form_cert
        INV-001: Certificate may not be unique (different quorum subsets possible)
        INV-002: Two valid certificates on same Tx are semantically identical
        INV-003: EffCert is a transferable proof of finality
        INV-004: Certificate for an object proves all dependent certificates in causal path are final
    end note
